From 7ded1b259b43508666db16d4072decd597ce050a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martino Facchin <m.facchin@arduino.cc>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:34:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: spi: stm32: pre-fill two packets in peripheral mode

In FIFO full-duplex mode only one packet (fifo-threshold bytes) is
queued in the TxFIFO before the transfer starts. As a peripheral the
controller sets the pace, so once that packet has been shifted out the
next one must already be in the TxFIFO: the DXP interrupt only fires
when the last byte has been received, leaving no time for the ISR to
refill the FIFO and causing a TxFIFO underrun.

On an STM32U585 (SPI3, 8-byte FIFO) this limited the peripheral to
about 100 kHz. Queue a second packet when there is room so the ISR has
one packet of slack; with st,fifo-threshold = <4> transfers now work
at 1 and 2 MHz.

Signed-off-by: Martino Facchin <m.facchin@arduino.cc>
---
 drivers/spi/spi_stm32.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi_stm32.c b/drivers/spi/spi_stm32.c
index 9733dbf4faa..3cb3e743949 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi_stm32.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi_stm32.c
@@ -926,6 +926,14 @@ static void spi_stm32_msg_start(const struct device *dev, bool is_rx_empty)
 				 * FIFO full until all data is sent.
 				 */
 				spi_stm32_send_fifo(spi, data);
+				/* As peripheral the controller sets the pace: queue one more
+				 * packet so the TxFIFO doesn't underrun while the DXP ISR is
+				 * pending.
+				 */
+				if (LL_SPI_GetMode(spi) == LL_SPI_MODE_SLAVE &&
+				    data->tx_len != 0U && ll_tx_is_not_full(spi)) {
+					spi_stm32_send_fifo(spi, data);
+				}
 				ll_enable_int_dxp(spi);
 #endif /* DT_HAS_COMPAT_STATUS_OKAY(st_stm32h7_spi) */
 			} else {
-- 
